The '''2007 FIFA Club World Cup''' (officially known as the '''FIFA Club World Cup Japan 2007 presented by [[Toyota]]''' for sponsorship reasons) was a [[association football|football]] tournament played in [[Japan]] from 7 to 16 December 2007. It was the fourth [[FIFA Club World Cup]], a tournament organised by [[FIFA]] for the winners of each confederation's top continental club tournament.

Seven teams from the six confederations entered the tournament; the other team was the host country's representatives, usually the league champions. Defending champions [[Sport Club Internacional|Internacional]] did not qualify as they were eliminated in the second stage of the [[2007 Copa Libertadores]]. 

Italian side [[AC Milan|Milan]] became the first European team to win the Club World Cup with a 4–2 victory over Argentinian club [[Boca Juniors]] in the [[2007 FIFA Club World Cup Final|final]]. That title made them the most successful team in the world in terms of official international trophies won (18). 

==Host bids==
The [[FIFA Executive Committee]] appointed Japan as hosts of the 2007 tournament on 15 September 2006 during their meeting in [[Zürich]], Switzerland.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.fifa.com/en/media/index/0%2C1369%2C122122%2C00.html |title=Code of Ethics approved – Lord Sebastian Coe to be chairman of Ethics Committee |publisher=[[FIFA]] |date=15 September 2006 |access-date=28 December 2022 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20061017034914/http://www.fifa.com/en/media/index/0,1369,122122,00.html |archive-date=17 October 2006}}</ref>

